ng-term  consumption of sugary beverages could  cause impaired learning  memory and behavioral plasticity other  studies have often found a link between  sugary drinks and an increased risk of  alzheimer's and other forms of dementia  cutting soda out of your diet will  drastically improve your overall brain  function and protect you from serious  memory conditions in the long term  in the short term you'll begin to feel  more awake and alert during the day once  you've broken your dependency on the  sugar and caffeine kick soda provides  your bones will also benefit from  quitting soda significantly lowering  your chances of developing osteoporosis  and other bone disorders  the acids and soda contribute to a  gradual weakening of your bones to the  point where breaks and fractures are  much more common  the less soda you drink the stronger  your bones will become  your kidney health will begin to improve  drastically studies have indicated that  drinking large amounts of soda can lead  to kidney disease and ultimately  complete kidney failure  to make things worse in some cases soft  drinks have been shown to contain bpa  which has been linked to an increase in  risk of breast and prostate cancer  premature puberty  infertility metabolic disorders and  diabetes  then of course there's obesity despite  all the serious health conditions soda  can cause  obesity gets the spotlight probably  because it's the most obvious side  effect  as everything else is happening behind  the scenes simply replacing soda with  water can make a huge difference in your  weight  drinking water first thing in the  morning kickstarts your metabolism  a study on obese children found that  drinking a glass of cold water raised  their resting energy expenditure by 25  percent  people who drink at least one to one and  a half liters of water per day for a few  weeks typically see a noticeable  reduction in weight  bmi and waist circumference your skin  will be clearer and smoother within  weeks  and adequate water intake helps to  prevent aging and all of this is just  the benefits of drinking water in  general  if you were to completely replace soda  with water the change in your overall  health would be dramatic  and you'd add years to your life in the  long term so if you want to avoid  diseases of every organ in the body  obesity and brittle bones maybe cut back  on the soda a bit  and try water instead here's a bit of  perspective to make transitioning to  water a little bit easier  just think of how fortunate we are to  even have such an abundance of clean  drinking water  when there are so many places around the  world where clean water is hard to come  by  if you want to help take two seconds to  install the new and improved tab for a  cause extension for your web browser  tab for a cause is a browser extension  that donates to a charity of your choice  each time you open a new tab without  costing you a thing  just by browsing the web tabbers have  now raised more than 450  thousand dollars for charity through tab  for a cause installing the extension  takes almost no effort and lets you make  a real difference every single day  just by using your web browser click the  link in the description to start tabbing  for your cause today  if you enjoyed this video consider  subscribing to support the channel and  click the little bell to join the  notification squad  you can watch my previous video by  clicking here or if you're really bored  you can binge watch all my content by  clicking here  thanks for watching and i'll see you  next week
 

